        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nWhere should I grab references to child nodes, and where does movement code go?",
          "label": "evals/godot/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "6b10d3871a3ae9409e361c8436837a73eb1b8329d7f905a90bac6c464312a875",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "Grab child references with `@onready` at the top of the script. Put movement in `_physics_process(delta)`.\n\n```gdscript\nextends CharacterBody2D\n\n@export var speed := 300.0\n\n@onready var sprite: Sprite2D = $Sprite2D\n@onready var anim: AnimationPlayer = $AnimationPlayer\n\nfunc _physics_process(delta: float) -> void:\n    var dir := Input.get_vector(\"left\", \"right\", \"up\", \"down\")\n    velocity = dir * speed\n    move_and_slide()\n```\n\n- **Why `@onready`:** children aren't in the tree until `_ready()` runs, so a plain `var x = $Child` initializer gets `null`. `@onready` runs the assignment right before `_ready()`.\n- **Why `_physics_process`:** `move_and_slide()` and other physics-body calls belong on the fixed physics tick. Use `_process` only for visuals.\n- **Child nodes:** for nodes that may be renamed or moved, prefer `@export var foo: Node` or a unique-name reference (`%Foo`) over a brittle `$A/B/C` path."
        },
